"""The service jobs this project runs on a schedule.

One list, read by the scheduler (which schedules each entry) and, in a stack
with a worker, by the worker (which registers each as a task named after its
function). The heartbeat is not here: it belongs to the scheduler itself.

To add a job, add an entry. Code is the source of truth: every scheduler
start re-registers each entry, so editing a trigger and redeploying changes
the schedule.
"""

